# Git repo Claude Code should use for `acpx` sessions (directory with `.git/`).
# Prefer the wiki-llm plugin repo root or a user project root — not `apps/web` alone,
# or set LLM_WIKI_PLUGIN_ROOT below so the desk can list installed skills.
ACP_WORKSPACE=/absolute/path/to/wiki-llm-or-your-project

# Required: shared secret for /api/chat and /api/config (constant-time compare on the server).
# Generate e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Bind the Next server to localhost only (see README).
# Do NOT deploy this app on a public/LAN host — anyone who can load the page sees the token.
ACP_WEB_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# Same value for the browser UI (Authorization / X-ACP-Web-Token). Required for the desk to load.
# Bundled into client JS by design for this localhost desk — treat as public to page visitors.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ACP_WEB_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# Optional: llm-wiki vault directory (default: <ACP_WORKSPACE>/llm-wiki).
# LLM_WIKI_VAULT=/absolute/path/to/llm-wiki

# wiki-llm plugin checkout (must contain skills/wiki-setup/SKILL.md). If unset, the
# server walks up from ACP_WORKSPACE to find it. Set explicitly when cwd is ambiguous.
# LLM_WIKI_PLUGIN_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/wiki-llm

# Allow POST /api/chat even when skills/ cannot be resolved (not recommended).
# ACP_WEB_SKIP_SKILL_CHECK=0

# Optional: override the acpx package spec passed to `npx` (default: acpx@latest).
# ACP_ACPX_PACKAGE=acpx@latest

# Optional: acpx permission mode (default: approve-reads). Also: approve-all | deny-all.
# ACP_ACPX_PERMISSION_MODE=approve-reads

# System prompt for the chat client (prepended into each acpx --file payload).
# Default file: apps/web/prompts/wiki-llm-chat-system.md (resolved from the Next app).
# ACP_SYSTEM_PROMPT_PATH=prompts/wiki-llm-chat-system.md

# Set to 1 to send only the user message with no system block (debug).
# ACP_SKIP_SYSTEM_PROMPT=0
